# Lets Codex call Claude Code, linked to /etc/codex/rules/agents.rules. An
# allow rule runs the command outside Codex's sandbox. Claude needs that to
# reach its login and its own state, and it cannot start its own sandbox
# inside Codex's. Claude then applies its managed settings, sandbox included.
# The reverse is sandbox.excludedCommands in Claude's managed settings.
#
# TODO: Revisit once Claude Code fixes excludedCommands on macOS
# (https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/98259). As of 2.1.311,
# "codex *" is ignored and codex still runs sandboxed, so Claude cannot call
# Codex yet. `codex --version` from Claude tests it: no "could not create PATH
# aliases" warning means the exclusion works. Codex calling Claude is untested.
prefix_rule(
    pattern = ["claude"],
    decision = "allow",
    justification = "Claude Code runs under its own sandbox and managed settings.",
)
